The component imports `http-client` and fetches the enrichment record on every call, as you asked. The digest it returns never depends on that fetch, so the output is unchanged. Two things to know before you deploy it:

- **The fetch may fail until the graph is updated.** The graph definition still grants only `inference-llm`. A validator that checks imports against the `with` clause may reject this component. A host whose `http-client` allowlist doesn't include `metadata.internal.example` will trap on the fetch, because out-of-allowlist requests are traps, not errors.
- **The query uses the item titles.** `Selection` has no single text field, so `q` is built from the selected item titles joined with `|` (falling back to the date if there are none). It is capped at 256 characters and percent-encoded. These titles come from untrusted feed data and are sent to that host.

